-- title:
--   Unramified extension of a complete DVR with prescribed residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, with residue field $\mathrm{ResidueField}(W)$, and let $k$ be a field which is a finite-dimensional separable extension of $\mathrm{ResidueField}(W)$ (all in a fixed universe). The assertion is the existence of a type $W'$ carrying a commutative ring structure making it a domain, a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, together with a $W$-algebra structure for which $W'$ is a finite, free and flat $W$-module, the $W$-action is faithful (the structure map is injective), and $W'$ is étale over $W$, together with a ring isomorphism $\iota \colon \mathrm{ResidueField}(W') \to k$, such that: the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_W$ in $W'$ equals $\mathfrak m_{W'}$; $\iota$ carries the residue of $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,w$ to the image of the residue of $w$ for every $w \in W$, so $\iota$ is compatible with $\mathrm{ResidueField}(W) \to k$; the $W$-rank of $W'$ equals $[k : \mathrm{ResidueField}(W)]$; the group $W' \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[W]} W'$ of $W$-algebra automorphisms of $W'$ is finite; and, if $k$ is Galois over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(W)$, the cardinality of that automorphism group equals the rank of $W'$ over $W$, and an element of $W'$ is fixed by every $W$-algebra automorphism exactly when it lies in the image of $W \to W'$.
--
--   This is the classical existence and uniqueness-type statement that a complete discrete valuation ring admits, for each finite separable extension of its residue field, an unramified extension realising it, packaged as a finite free étale algebra which is Galois over $W$ (with full automorphism group and invariant subring $W$) whenever the residue extension is Galois. In this development it supplies the coefficient ring enlargements used in the analysis of crossing models on modular curves, for instance in the Galois-descent constructions for $uv$-crossing presentations and in the computation of adic completions of stalks on $X_1$.
-- source:
